#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046644} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515683} :activity/id #uuid "f434441f-b9c7-5ee6-aaa1-b1b2afd5d471" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049381 :topic/id #uuid "f0242aed-46fd-5f2e-bcc2-49ee070cdccf" :topic/math-academy-id 3190} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515627 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515593 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53cfc804-f2be-5e9c-8d5c-d7bbbd137c44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{-{s}^{2}+2s+3}{s(s-2)(s-4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515056}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515056} :answer-field/id #uuid "029ce416-5248-5a5e-a914-f27e3f878e0b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515411}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c20fd0ed-71f4-5fd0-a6bc-687a270c962b" :question/math-academy-id "q-333060" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2s-3}{s(s-4)}$ ,$\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{4{x}_{1}(t)-3\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=4L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-3L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2=4{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1=-{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2 & =4{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =2-\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2s-3}{s} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2s-3}{s(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)+1 & =-{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =-{X}_{1}(s)-1 \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =-(\\frac{2s-3}{s(s-4)})-1 \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-(2s-3)-s(s-4)}{s(s-4)} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-2s+3-{s}^{2}+4s}{s(s-4)} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+2s+3}{s(s-4)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+2s+3}{s(s-2)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2s-3}{s(s-4)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-{s}^{2}+2s+3}{s(s-2)(s-4)}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0d621a8f-cd0d-51e8-81b6-9ebdb390477f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515697}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515656 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308393 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "836205cc-5a3f-59ff-b85b-57b4914eb6b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}+2-2{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306406}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306406} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a865178-7308-51f1-b0b9-0385a7f16eef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308008} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "330e1019-3a7b-578b-a870-9a3ed163159a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1+{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305632}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305632} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7279e72-7b0d-5ec9-8874-4267900baa48" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "94146fce-5a5d-5f8d-9ed4-34e48238a883" :question/math-academy-id "q-333138" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+6{x}_{2}(t)+2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{2}(t)-1,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=-\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}+\\frac{2}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s+1}-\\frac{1}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{-\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}+\\frac{2}{s}} \\\\  & =-2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}+2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-1\\cdot t}+{e}^{2\\cdot t}+2 \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}+2-2{e}^{-t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}-\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & =-1+{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+2-2{e}^{-t} \\\\ -1+{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "590ff66c-34e8-5381-aeda-9ccba67a75bc"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515683 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515576 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e75c2a5-efac-57be-8e90-38a4d983daed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-2)(s-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515132}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515132} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbc222a5-fba5-54b1-8499-8bdfb1e8616c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "95759fde-a83b-52c8-a112-ac2f3137ea76" :question/math-academy-id "q-332776" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-4 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-2)},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)-4\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-4L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-3=2{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-0={X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-3 & =2{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{1}(s) & =3-\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3s-4}{s} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s) & ={X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & ={X}_{1}(s) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-2)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-1)(s-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system  in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-2)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-1)(s-2)}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b1745bc0-7e7d-5cce-a4e0-1fadf2d21096" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515627}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515690 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308390 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43cd4f5c-08fd-5bbb-8ca5-7564ab540dcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305818}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305818} :answer-field/id #uuid "a11cf526-3ad2-5d27-b464-c2dc1021fed5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308033} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb7af99f-f087-5140-92ed-ce44ed5c2329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{e}^{2t}+{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306897}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306897} :answer-field/id #uuid "d625bed8-e9e7-5e12-a73f-2e476aeb6a2e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308191}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "12cb134e-509f-512f-9761-fbb450604687" :question/math-academy-id "q-333133" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+9{x}_{2}(t)+9 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{2}(t)+2,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{3}{s-2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{3}{s-2}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}+3\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1\\cdot t}+3{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}+3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3{e}^{2t}+{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}-1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "c1ab16a5-ba62-5d1f-b985-9e65b24b08aa" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515656}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515697 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515563 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81d22d6e-0616-586f-b9f3-42b8d530fd5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{2t}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515140}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515140} :answer-field/id #uuid "0560274e-eedd-5cd3-a9f0-b7e672a7b4b9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515412} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f2f8e1b-7ba5-5978-8caf-e60c554b76cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2e^{2t}+e^{3t}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515209}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515209} :answer-field/id #uuid "49de807c-da2e-59f0-b447-3aed1873fc9c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515434}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "78ae591d-ba8b-5d77-97cc-75f76d82b6a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-333128" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+4 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)-5,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=-\\frac{2}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s-3}+\\frac{3}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}-2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\cdot t}-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{-\\frac{2}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s-3}+\\frac{3}{s}\\} \\\\  & =-2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\}+3\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2\\cdot t}+{e}^{3\\cdot t}+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}-2{e}^{2t}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}-2 \\\\ {e}^{3t}-2{e}^{2t}+3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "cd1c018d-a850-5621-b116-c5c0cc1a8c99" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515690}}] :activity/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Laplace Transforms" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514867}]}
